LIMIT: the sink is in-process and the checkpoint is a plain file, so this shows the ordering contract (commit, then checkpoint) rather than real durability. A crash between the sink commit and the checkpoint write still re-delivers that one slot, which is why the sink write must be idempotent on slot. No gRPC, reconstruction or real provider.
